# Scenes

One file per scene. Copy [`_template.md`](_template.md) when adding a new one.

**Naming convention:** `NNN-short-name.md` — three-digit zero-padded number so the directory sorts in story order. Renumber freely as the story shifts.

## Chapter mapping convention

The default workflow is **one scene per chapter**. In that case:

- Each scene has its own `chapter:` number (`chapter: 1`, `chapter: 2`, ...).
- The scene's `name` field doubles as the chapter title at compile time — no `chapter_title:` needed.

When you later combine two or more scenes into a single chapter:

- Give them the same `chapter:` number.
- Add `chapter_title: "..."` to one of those scenes (first occurrence in scene-number order wins).
- The `compile-manuscript` skill will warn if you have a multi-scene chapter without a `chapter_title:`.

